[Desktop Entry]
# Spotify: its web player (open.spotify.com) in a window of its own — Helium's app window: no
# tabs, no address bar, tiled like every other window, through ~/.local/bin/kawa-browser as
# all of Helium is. Free or Premium, signed in once (Helium keeps the login). It plays through
# Helium, so the bar's now-playing and its meter show it (Helium's media session over MPRIS,
# cava on the output) and the media keys work it. Spotify's player needs Widevine, which the
# toolkit fetches from Google and kawa-browser names to Helium (lib/upstream.sh). Its
# icon: our pixel music (the launcher draws it: X-Fedokawaii-Icon).
Type=Application
Name=Spotify
GenericName=Music Player
Comment=Spotify's web player, in a window of its own
X-Fedokawaii-Icon=music
Exec=@HOME@/.local/bin/kawa-browser --app=https://open.spotify.com
Terminal=false
Categories=Audio;AudioVideo;Player;
Keywords=spotify;music;songs;podcasts;
